# R23 the funny people of the eve: Gaunt, Quill, Pip and Barnaby. By hand, polished by Gemini, unvoiced.

~ gaunt
sgt_gaunt [smile]: Sergeant Gaunt, rear guard. Do not worry about the line. I am behind it, and I have it in hand.
-> gaunt_menu

~ gaunt_menu
* [if item:wv_last_letters and not flag.letter_gaunt] Give him the letter from his mother -> vigil/letters:to_gaunt
* Ask how the rear guard is positioned -> gaunt_position
* Ask for a word of advice -> gaunt_advice
* Wish him luck -> END

~ gaunt_position
sgt_gaunt [neutral]: Behind the barricade, behind the line, behind the village, and, if the wind is right, behind the hill. A good soldier always has something between him and the enemy. Preferably a village.
-> gaunt_menu

~ gaunt_advice
sgt_gaunt [sly]: When the line breaks, fall back to a strong position. When the strong position breaks, fall back to a stronger one. I have been falling back for thirty years and I have never once been caught.
-> gaunt_menu

~ quill
ambrose_quill [smile]: The village is about to be burned, and I have finished the elegy. It scans. It has a good chorus. I call it "Lament for the Round", and by the third verse it is, I fear, a hymn for charging.
-> quill_menu

~ quill_menu
* Ask him to recite it -> quill_elegy
* [if flag.wv_vol_asked and not flag.vol_quill] Ask him to sign the militia roll -> quill_sign
* [if item:wv_last_letters and not flag.letter_quill] Give him the letter from the publisher -> vigil/letters:to_quill
* Leave him to his rhymes -> END

~ quill_elegy
Narrator: He clears his throat, stands on a bench, and reads. The first stanza mourns the village. The second mourns the dead. By the third it is rhyming "foe" with "go", and by the fourth the bucket line has started marching in step.
if not flag.quill_blessed
Narrator: Something rises in your chest that has no business in an elegy. It is, unmistakably, a battle hymn.
bless party 2h
set quill_blessed
endif
-> quill_menu

~ quill_sign
ambrose_quill [sad]: I will sign, if the roll will record that my elegy is the regimental hymn. It is only fair. It is the only one that exists.
* [Performance DC 13] Tell him the hymn will go in the margin, with a flourish -> quill_signed | quill_sulk
* Promise to put it in the roll yourself -> quill_signed

~ quill_signed
Narrator: He signs with a flourish that takes up the whole margin, and underlines it twice.
set vol_quill
set vol_signed += 1
-> quill_menu

~ quill_sulk
ambrose_quill [sad]: I fear that was not a flourish. It was a shrug.
-> quill_sign

~ pip
pip_oakum [smile]: I have one hundred and twelve buttons and I am going to trade them for courage. Whose is the best? I will give you three buttons for the best.
-> pip_menu

~ pip_menu
* Ask about the buttons -> pip_buttons
* [if not flag.pip_traded] Trade for his courage button -> pip_trade
* Wish him luck -> END

~ pip_buttons
pip_oakum [neutral]: This one is from a hero's coat. This one is from a dead man's shirt. This one is from the door of the church, and it is warm. The warm one is the best one.
-> pip_menu

~ pip_trade
pip_oakum [smile]: You can have the warm one. In return I want to know that you will come back, and tell me what it was like.
Narrator: He presses a brass button into your hand. It is warm, as he said.
give wv_pip_button
inspiration party
set pip_traded
-> pip_menu

~ barnaby
barnaby_pennywhistle [smile]: Wicker Man repellent! Two gold for a bottle, five for a case, free for the infirm and the brave. Guaranteed against wicker, men, and, as of this afternoon, Wicker Men. The third is new.
-> barnaby_menu

~ barnaby_menu
* [if gold >= 5 and not flag.barnaby_sold] Buy a bottle for five gold -> barnaby_buy
* [if flag.wv_vol_asked and not flag.vol_barnaby] Ask him to sign the militia roll -> barnaby_sign
* Ask what is in it -> barnaby_what
* Leave him to his trade -> END

~ barnaby_what
barnaby_pennywhistle [sly]: Mostly vinegar. Some cider. A little of something that I cannot name for legal reasons. The label is the important part.
-> barnaby_menu

~ barnaby_buy
barnaby_pennywhistle [smile]: A discerning customer. Shake well. Do not drink. Spray liberally at the thing you wish it not to do.
gold -5
give wv_barnaby_repellent
set barnaby_sold
-> barnaby_menu

~ barnaby_sign
barnaby_pennywhistle [neutral]: A volunteer? I am a vendor. Vendors are not volunteers. But if the roll records a bulk order, I will sign.
* [Persuasion DC 13] Argue that a vendor is a volunteer who has not yet been paid -> barnaby_signed | barnaby_no
* Promise to put a bulk order on the roll -> barnaby_signed

~ barnaby_signed
Narrator: He signs with the air of a man who has read the small print and found it his own.
set vol_barnaby
set vol_signed += 1
-> barnaby_menu

~ barnaby_no
barnaby_pennywhistle [sad]: Splendid logic. I am afraid it is also wrong.
-> barnaby_sign
